# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# requirements-watcher.in — the crypto trigger watcher's dependency set.
#
# Why this file exists: check-triggers-crypto.yml runs scripts/check_triggers.py
# --crypto-only hourly, 24/7. Installing the full requirements.txt for it took
# 48s of an 87s job whose actual work is ~6s — and GitHub bills every job rounded
# UP to a whole minute, so that overhead was doubling the bill for every run.
# The full lockfile carries matplotlib, scikit-learn, numba, plotly, streamlit,
# fastapi, bt and pytest; the crypto path imports none of them.
#
# These four are the measured minimum: import scripts.check_triggers fails
# without any of them (yfinance and pandas arrive transitively through
# engine.corporate_actions and engine.quotes, not from the watcher directly).
#
# Same discipline as requirements.in → requirements.txt: this is the loose
# source, requirements-watcher.txt is the pinned lockfile, and every pin in it
# MUST equal the root lockfile's. tests/test_ci_guards.py enforces that — a
# watcher running different versions from the desk is a silent divergence on
# the money path.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

